course: dictionary
lesson: 14702
title: Printmakers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A printmaker is an artist who makes pictures by printing. Printing means pressing ink onto paper, so one picture can be copied many times. «The printmaker carved a fish into a block of wood.» The word has two parts, print and maker, so a printmaker is a person who makes prints.
explain: Look for clues. «She rolled ink onto her lino and pressed it onto the paper.» Rolling ink and pressing it onto paper is printing, so she is a printmaker. Ask yourself: is this artist making a picture by printing? If yes, the word fits.
explain: Printmakers use different methods, such as woodcuts, lino prints, etchings and screen prints. Each one is a kind of printing, and the person who makes it is a printmaker.
fact: A printmaker is an artist who makes pictures by printing.
fact: Common printing methods include woodcuts, lino prints, etchings and screen prints.
fact: In art lessons, children are printmakers when they make lino or polystyrene prints with ink and rollers.
fact: Albrecht Dürer and Katsushika Hokusai are famous printmakers.
fact: «The Great Wave» is a famous print made by the printmaker Hokusai.
exercise: «The printmaker rolled ink onto the lino block.» What is a printmaker? | A machine that cuts wood | A person who sells paper in a shop | *An artist who makes pictures by printing
exercise: «Maya made a polystyrene print of a tree in art class.» What is Maya in this sentence? | A photographer who takes pictures | A bus driver | A sculptor who carves stone | *A printmaker
exercise: Which of these is a kind of print a printmaker might make? | Knitted scarf | *Lino print | Clay pot | Pencil sketch on a notepad
test: «Hokusai was a famous printmaker.» What does printmaker mean? | A worker who repairs computers | A person who paints walls | A teacher who runs a printing shop | *An artist who makes pictures by printing
test: Which two artists are named as famous printmakers in this lesson? | *Albrecht Dürer and Katsushika Hokusai | Isaac Newton and Marie Curie | Pablo Picasso and Vincent van Gogh | Leonardo da Vinci and Claude Monet
exam: «A printmaker uses ink and a tool to press a picture onto paper.» Which tool helps a printmaker spread ink? | A kettle | A pencil sharpener | *An ink roller | A ruler
